# 093 · Live shows what the model thinks and says, not only its tool calls

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.2.0](../roadmap.md#v020)

## What

A bug fix. **Live** for a run shows each agent's turn as an agent harness shows it: the model's reasoning (when the model gives it), its words between tool calls, and then the calls and their results. Today a worker's Live shows mostly its tool calls (many fetches, for example), and the model's thinking about what to call next is missing.

- Find where each harness's stream (Pi, OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex) gives reasoning and text, and pass it to Live, shortened as Live shortens other lines, with a way to open a line in full.
- Reasoning is the agent's own text: it is treated as data, never as instructions, as other agent text is, and it never carries a held-out case.
- A filter on Live to show or hide reasoning lines.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-22, watching a worker in Live: "I see tons of fetches. But I don't see any model reasoning etc that you see on typical harnesses as the model is thinking about what to call etc... Seems I don't see all the live data there is."

## Done when

- [ ] Live shows each harness's reasoning and text lines where the model gives them, with tests for each harness's stream.
- [ ] The pages that describe Live.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-22, owner: a bug fix for v0.1.1.
- 2026-10-24, owner: v0.1.1 becomes the code clean-up; this goal moves to v0.1.4, the UI clean-up and UX improvements.

## Open questions

- How much reasoning to keep in control's Live store (it can be long), and whether exports keep it.

## Progress

- 2026-10-22: Goal written from the owner's feedback.

